  "materials": [
    "Mouse anti-GluN1 monoclonal antibody",
    "Goat anti-mouse Alexa fluor 488 antibody",
    "Tricaine (MS-222)",
    "Ficoll PM 400",
    "Sodium chloride",
    "Potassium chloride",
    "Sodium bicarbonate",
    "Calcium chloride",
    "HEPES free acid",
    "UltraPure RNase-free distilled water",
    "Human chorionic gonadotropin (hCG)",
    "Pregnant mare serum gonadotropin (PMSG)",
    "All-Digital Multi-Pressure microINJECTOR",
    "Singer “Pantographic” Micromanipulator, MK-1",
    "P-97 flaming/brown micropipette puller",
    "GeneJet PCR purification kit",
    "Timing: 3 h\n1.Prepare the following solutions:a.0.1× modified Barth’s solution with HEPES buffer (MBSH) for rearing animals.b.1× MBSH for storing male frog testes and preparing Ficoll solution.c.0.2% MS-222 in 0.1× MBSH for tadpole and frog euthanasia.d.0.02% MS-222 in 0.1× MBSH for tadpole anaesthesia.e.2% Ficoll in 1× MBSH for blastomere injection.f.1% Ficoll in 0.1× MBSH for embryo incubation.\nNote: For countries where MS-222 is not permitted for adult euthanasia, intracoelomic pentobarbital (60 to 100 mg/kg body weight) can be used.\n2.Prepare the embryo injection chamber (Figure 2).\nNote: The injection chamber is composed of a plastic ring designed to fit inside a 60 mm diameter petri dish, with a square mesh with 1.2–1.4 mm spacing attached to the bottom to line up eggs for injection. The chamber can be 3D printed with the 3D print file provided at https://github.com/RuthazerLab/Hemimosaic-3d-models. Print the part with a raft with settings of 1.2–1.4 mm spacing and 0.8 mm thickness to produce the bottom mesh. Use PLA or an equivalent nontoxic filament."
  ],
  "steps": [
    {
      "step_id": 0,
      "title": "Prepare MBSH solutions",
      "instruction": "Make the following modified Barth’s solutions (MBSH): (a) 0.1× MBSH with HEPES for rearing animals; (b) 1× MBSH for storing male frog testes and for preparing Ficoll solutions.",
      "substeps": [],
      "is_critical": false,
      "timers": []
    },
    {
      "step_id": 1,
      "title": "Prepare MS-222 solutions",
      "instruction": "Prepare two MS-222 solutions in 0.1× MBSH: (c) 0.2% MS-222 for tadpole and frog euthanasia; (d) 0.02% MS-222 for tadpole anaesthesia. For regions where MS-222 is prohibited, use intracoelomic pentobarbital at 60–100 mg/kg body weight for euthanasia.",
      "substeps": [],
      "is_critical": false,
      "timers": []
    },
    {
      "step_id": 2,
      "title": "Prepare Ficoll solutions",
      "instruction": "Make two Ficoll solutions: (e) 2% Ficoll in 1× MBSH for blastomere injection; (f) 1% Ficoll in 0.1× MBSH for embryo incubation by dissolving 1 g Ficoll powder in 100 mL 0.1× MBSH, then store at 4 °C for up to 4 months.",
      "substeps": [],
      "is_critical": false,
      "timers": []
    },
    {
      "step_id": 3,
      "title": "Assemble injection chamber",
      "instruction": "Construct the embryo injection chamber: fit a plastic ring inside a 60 mm diameter petri dish and attach a square mesh with 1.2–1.4 mm spacing to line up eggs. The chamber can be 3D‑printed using the file at https://github.com/RuthazerLab/Hemimosaic-3d-models, printing with a raft, mesh spacing 1.2–1.4 mm, thickness 0.8 mm, and PLA or equivalent nontoxic filament.",
      "substeps": [],
      "is_critical": false,
      "timers": []
    }
  ],
